
microrom IPL and FC analysis of 17 bit microwords
microword:
Bit 16:         FC1
Bit 15:         FC0
Bit 14 - 5:     pointer to next micro word, format: 9 8 1 0 5 4 3 2 7 6
Bit 4, 3, 2, 1: control -> check fx68k for full description (will be used downwards)
Bit 0:          IRC->IR and latch IPL

the FC's in micro word are not in all cases the PIN outputs, because of PC relative addressing.
PCRel is seted from source EA field, not destination EA field in case of move instruction

FC1 = M16 | ( ~M15 & PCRel)
FC0 = M15 | ( ~M16 & ~PCRel)

M16 M15 PCRel   PIN out
0   0   0       FC1: 0, FC0: 1     internal or when reading from address (d8,An,Xn) and (d16,An)
0   1   0       FC1: 0, FC0: 1     reading/writing address
1   0   0       FC1: 1, FC0: 0     prefetch, read extension word
0   0   1       FC1: 1, FC0: 0     internal or when reading from PC rel address (d8,PC,Xn) and (d16,PC)
0   1   1       FC1: 0, FC0: 1     reading/writing address
1   0   1       FC1: 1, FC0: 0     prefetch, read extension word

1   1   0|1     makes no sense and not in microcode


